506		The line-point distribution places weight $\tfrac{1}{2}$ on each of the
507		axis-parallel and diagonal components and, within each component, uniform
508		weight on the index $i$, so each restricted distribution carries mixture
509		weight $\tfrac{1}{2m}$ in $D_{\mathrm{Line}}$. A nonnegative average that
510		is at most $\delta$ therefore bounds each mixture component by
511		$2m\delta$, and products of two such mixtures give the factor
512		$(2m)^2 = 4m^2$. The instance \eqref{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted} is item
513		2 applied to the conclusion of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines}, whose
514		$\simeq_{\delta_P}$ relation over two independent copies of the
